id: 14
hanzi: 杀
pinyin: shā
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Verb

meanings_summary:
  en: to kill; to slaughter; to terminate; to fight; to reduce
  es: matar; asesinar; sacrificar; exterminar; reducir

senses[4]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Verb | Standard | to deprive of life; to slaughter an animal or kill a person | matar; quitar la vida a una persona o sacrificar un animal | 杀鸡宰鹅 (slaughter chickens and geese)
  2 | Verb | Standard | to combat, defeat, or eliminate microorganisms, germs, or pests | exterminar gérmenes, parásitos o plagas | 杀菌消毒 (sterilize and kill bacteria)
  3 | Verb | Colloquial | to cut, reduce, or slash prices sharply | reducir o rebajar drásticamente precios | 杀价 (bargain down prices)
  4 | Verb | Colloquial | to dash, charge, or plunge into an action or place | irrumpir; lanzarse rápidamente hacia un lugar | 杀出重围 (fight one's way out of encirclement)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 依照民间传统，除夕清晨各家各户都会杀鸡宰鱼，准备丰盛的贡品祭祀祖先、祈求来年平安。 | Yīzhào mínjiān chuántǒng, Chúxī qīngchén gèjiā-gèhù dōu huì shā jī zǎi yú, zhǔnbèi fēngshèng de gòngpǐn jìsì zǔxiān, qíqiú láinián píng'ān. | According to folk traditions, on the morning of New Year's Eve, every household slaughters chickens and fish to prepare lavish offerings to venerate ancestors and pray for peace in the coming year. | Conforme a la tradición popular, en la mañana de nochevieja cada hogar sacrifica pollos y limpia pescado para preparar abundantes ofrendas dedicadas a los antepasados y pedir paz para el año venidero.
  #2 | 生物医药实验室在新型抗生素研发中，成功筛选出一种能高效杀灭多重耐药性病菌的活性化合物。 | Shēngwù yīyào shíyànshì zài xīnxíng kàngshēngsù yánfā zhōng, chénggōng shāixuǎn chū yì zhǒng néng gāoxiào shāmiè duōzhòng nàiyàoxìng bìngjūn de huóxìng huàhéwù. | In the development of new antibiotics, the biomedical laboratory successfully screened an active compound capable of efficiently eradicating multiple drug-resistant bacteria. | En la investigación de nuevos antibióticos, el laboratorio biomédico logró seleccionar un compuesto activo capaz de exterminar con alta eficacia bacterias con resistencia a múltiples fármacos.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  杀灭病菌 | eradicate pathogenic bacteria; kill germs
  杀价 | bargain down prices; slash price
  杀鸡取卵 | kill the hen to get the eggs (ruin source of gain)
  杀出重围 | break through an encirclement; carve a way out
  宰杀牲畜 | slaughter livestock
  杀伤力 | lethality; damaging power

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  杀鸡儆猴 | shā jī jǐng hóu | kill the chicken to warn the monkey; punish one to warn others
  杀身成仁 | shā shēn chéng rén | sacrifice one's life for benevolence; die for a noble cause
  借刀杀人 | jiè dāo shā rén | murder with a borrowed knife; harm someone through a third party
  杀一儆百 | shā yī jǐng bǎi | execute one to warn a hundred; make an example of one

character_decomposition[1]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  杀 | shā | kill; slaughter; eliminate; destroy | matar; asesinar; sacrificar; extinguir | 木 | wood / spear shaft | 木 (wooden lance or post) | 乂 (scythe slashing stroke / phonetic guide) | 6 | 上下结构 | Simplified from traditional 殺. The ancient oracle script showed a weapon striking an animal. Modern simplification unites crossing blade strokes (乂) falling down upon a wooden stake (木). | Crossing blades slashing in an X (乂) strike down forcefully against a wooden post (木) to slaughter a dangerous beast. | Hojas afiladas cruzadas en aspa (乂) descienden con fuerza letal sobre un poste de madera (木) para abatir a la fiera. | 55 | KCD | 殺

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Crossing blade strokes (乂) plunge into a wooden stake (木) to decisively slay and kill (杀) the threatening beast.
  composite_memory_hook_es: Filos cortantes cruzados en aspa (乂) se clavan sobre una estaca de madera (木) para matar (杀) y abatir a la bestia.
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In ancient mythology, the end of the year was associated with driving away or slaying (杀/驱) ferocious monsters like Nian (年兽) that threatened village survival. In classical thought, 杀 embodies both the stern, harvesting autumn energy (秋气主杀) and the legal sovereign power over life and death.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: High level 1st tone 'shā' (55). Maintain a sustained, steady pitch at the top of the vocal register without dipping before subsequent syllables.

traps_and_cognates:
