    杂 | zá | mixed; miscellaneous | Has 九 on top of 木 instead of 乂
    条 | tiáo | strip; item; branch | Has 夂 on top of 木 instead of 乂
    刹 | chà | temple; brake (shā) | Has 杀 on the left and knife radical 刂 on the right
    亲 | qīn | parent; intimate | Has 立 on top of 木 instead of 乂
    希 | xī | hope; rare | Has 爻 / 乂 with cloth radical 巾 below instead of 木
  etymological_cognates[5]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    宰 | zǎi | slaughter; butcher; govern
    屠 | tú | slaughter; massacre
    灭 | miè | extinguish; wipe out
    诛 | zhū | execute; punish severely
    戮 | lù | slaughter; massacre

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 杀 is the primary general verb meaning to deliberately terminate life or violently eliminate organisms or threats.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 杀 vs. 宰 | zǎi | 杀 is the broad, generic term for taking any life (human, beast, germ), whereas 宰 specifically denotes the methodical butchering and slaughtering of domestic livestock and poultry for food or sacrifice.
    2 | 杀 vs. 害 | hài | 杀 denotes the definitive act of causing physical death, whereas 害 means to harm, injure, impair, or bring misfortune without necessarily resulting in death (as in 伤害).
    3 | 杀 vs. 灭 | miè | 杀 focuses on the physical termination of individual living beings or entities, whereas 灭 emphasizes total annihilation, wiping out of an entire category, lineage, or extinguishing fires and lights (e.g. 消灭、灭亡).

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 民间传说中，远古怪兽年常在岁末残害生灵。乡民们燃起爆竹、点亮红烛，合力击退并诛杀恶兽，迎来了新春的黎明。除夕除害的传统，寄托了先民战胜严酷自然、渴望和平安宁的朴素信念。 | Mínjiān chuánshuō zhōng, yuǎngǔ guàishòu Nián cháng zài suìmò cánhài shēnglíng. Xiāngmínmen ránqǐ bàozhú, diǎnliàng hóngzhú, hélì jītuì bìng zhūshā èshòu, yínglái le xīnchūn de límíng. Chúxī chúhài de chuántǒng, jìtuō le xiānmín zhànshèng yánkù zìrán, kěwàng hépíng-ānníng de pùsù xìnniàn. | In folk legends, the ancient monster Nian frequently harmed living beings at year's end. Villagers lit firecrackers and red candles, joining forces to repel and slay the evil beast, ushering in the dawn of the new year. The tradition of eliminating perils on New Year's Eve reflects ancient people's simple faith in overcoming harsh nature and longing for peace. | En las leyendas populares, la fiera Nian solía dañar a las gentes a finales de año. Los aldeanos encendían petardos y velas rojas, uniendo fuerzas para repeler y matar a la bestia, dando la bienvenida al amanecer del nuevo año. La tradición de eliminar males en nochevieja refleja la fe ancestral en vencer la hostil naturaleza y hallar paz.
  #2 | 在现代农业病虫害综合防治体系中，过度依赖广谱化学农药虽能迅速杀灭有害昆虫，但也容易破坏农田生态链。推广生物防治与靶向杀菌技术，既能有效控制病害传播，又能守护土壤生态与食品安全底线。 | Zài xiàndài nóngyè bìngchónghài zōnghé fángzhì tǐxì zhōng, guòdù yīlài guǎngpǔ huàxué nóngyào suī néng xùnsù shāmiè yǒuhài kūnchóng, yě róngyì pòhuài nóngtián shēngtàiliàn. Tuīguǎng shēngwù fángzhì yǔ bǎxiàng shājūn jìshù, jìnìng yǒuxiào kòngzhì bìnghài chuánbō, yòu néng shǒuhù tǔrǎng shēngtài yǔ shípǐn ānquán dǐxiàn. | In modern integrated agricultural pest management systems, excessive reliance on broad-spectrum chemical pesticides can quickly kill harmful insects, but easily damages farmland ecological chains. Promoting biological control and targeted sterilization technology effectively curtails disease transmission while safeguarding soil ecology and food safety baselines. | En el manejo fitosanitario agrícola moderno, el abuso de pesticidas químicos de amplio espectro extermina rápidamente insectos dañinos, pero altera la cadena ecológica. Fomentar el control biológico y la esterilización dirigida frena eficazmente la propagación de plagas y protege el suelo y la seguridad alimentaria.
